<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zhangsun Sheng</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">551–609</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zhangsun Sheng was a Chinese general and diplomat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-zhou">Northern Zhou</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui</a> dynasties who specialised in relations with the Turks. Having lived at the Turkic court, he advised the Sui founder Emperor Wen to divide the khaganate by backing rival khans, summed up as befriending the distant and attacking the near. His policy helped split the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-turkic-khaganate">First Turkic Khaganate</a> into eastern and western halves.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zhangsun-sheng.jpg" alt="Zhangsun Sheng" width="320" height="457" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ma Tai (馬駘; 1885-1937) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E4%B8%80%E7%AE%AD%E9%9B%99%E9%9B%95.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
